813790083, "top": [[" compiler", -0.006601798813790083], [" Compiler", -5.075336933135986]]}, {"t": "**", "lp": -0.00022741757857147604, "top": [["**", -0.00022741757857147604], [" =", -10.539669036865234]]}, {"t": " \u2014", "lp": -0.0017903370317071676, "top": [[" \u2014", -0.0017903370317071676], [" use", -7.307332515716553]]}, {"t": " use", "lp": -0.24696917831897736, "top": [[" use", -0.24696917831897736], [" Intel", -1.5242176055908203]]}, {"t": " Intel", "lp": -0.0006909372750669718, "top": [[" Intel", -0.0006909372750669718], [" the", -7.485897541046143]]}, {"t": "'s", "lp": -0.0883912518620491, "top": [["'s", -0.0883912518620491], [" one", -2.8742799758911133]]}, {"t": " `", "lp": -0.21096138656139374, "top": [[" `", -0.21096138656139374], [" C", -2.4213876724243164]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -0.0002503112191334367, "top": [["ic", -0.0002503112191334367], [" ic", -9.729657173156738]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're using Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, which need their environment configured to work.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so the build stops on failure rather than continuing with broken state.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **Source directory** \u2014 where the source code lives (the git clone). |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **Build directory** \u2014 where build artifacts go (out-of-source build). |\n| `-G Ninja` | **Generator** \u2014 use Ninja as the build system (fast, efficient). |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | **Optimization** \u2014 compile with optimizations enabled (`-O3`-like flags). |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | **Install location** \u2014 where files will be installed (`/usr`). |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | **Library subdir** \u2014 put libraries in `/usr/lib` (not `/usr/lib64`). |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | **C compiler** \u2014 use Intel's `ic"}